# React + TypeScript Best Practices

- Prefer functional components with hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`, `useMemo`, `useCallback`).
- Strong typing: define component props and state with explicit interfaces/types.
- Keep components small and focused; lift state up or extract hooks for shared logic.
- Memoize expensive computations (`useMemo`) and stable callbacks (`useCallback`) for perf.
- Derive UI strictly from props/state; avoid side effects in render.
- Handle API data with typed clients and error states; avoid implicit any.
- Use Suspense-friendly patterns where applicable; keep loading/error states consistent.
- Keep CSS scoped (CSS Modules or CSS-in-JS) and avoid global leakage.
- Avoid inline functions in hot lists; memoize list items with `key`.
